  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GBV Response Risk mitigation East Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project UNFPA improves the access of displaced women to GBV response services in the areas affected by the flood in the East of Libya. This includes: establishment of temporary and semi-permanent Women and Girls Safe Spaces (WGSS) in IDP-hosting areas; procurement and distribution of 4,000 Dignity Kits as part of GBV risk mitigation activities; distribution of core relief items to the displaced populations through the RRM; deployment of mobile social worker teams to provide mental health and psycho-social support to affected people. The agency targets 4,299 affected people through this Protection (GBV) project.</narrative>
  </description>
